cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use crypto-service-sdk-rust in research or production write-ups, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "crypto-service-sdk-rust: a typed Rust client for the Crypto Service REST API"
abstract: >-
  An async and blocking, typed Rust client for the v2 REST API of
  crypto-server: hashing, AEAD, server-held keys, ML-KEM, ML-DSA,
  SLH-DSA, HPKE, KMS and OPAQUE. A thin client with no cryptography of
  its own, it runs the shared Crypto Service conformance kit against a
  live server.
authors:
  - family-names: Rousseau
    given-names: Sebastien
version: "0.0.41"
# Dual-licensed, at the user's option (LICENSE-APACHE, LICENSE-MIT). CFF
# 1.2.0 takes SPDX licence identifiers, not an SPDX expression; a list of
# several means the work is available under any of them.
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/crypto-service-sdk-rust"
url: "https://crypto-service.co"
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - post-quantum
  - ML-KEM
  - KMS
  - Rust
